# gRPC plugins (host vs binary)

Plugins are **separate processes** (`internal/plugin` + `sdk/plugin`). This is not the in-tree NIP registry. Full decision record: [docs/plugin-architecture.md](docs/plugin-architecture.md).

- Plugins import **only** `github.com/michmich112/congee/sdk/plugin`. Never the parent module.
- **Listen** is non-blocking enqueue after an in-process match. **Intercept** is the only sync RPC; not-ready / timeout / RPC error **fail-open** (plugin never called).
- **Intercept log** stays on the **host**: copy after intercept returns, logging goroutine, drop-on-full. Do not add it to proto, Conduit, or the plugin iframe.
- Plugin iframe: `connect-src 'none'`, no `allow-same-origin`, no admin token. Host chrome owns intercept-log GET/PUT.

```
// ❌ BAD — plugin-only log misses fail-open; iframe cannot fetch admin API
// ✅ GOOD — host enqueueInterceptLog after doIntercept; InterceptLogPanel on the settings page
```
